# Requests to the api for the REST Client extension. No secrets in this file.
# Start the api first (`bb dev`, or `(go)` in the REPL). To call protected endpoints, run
# `bb token <username>` (or `bb token scheduler`) in a terminal and paste the result into
# @token below; access tokens last 5 minutes. Demo users: see tools/realm.clj.

@api = http://localhost:4000
@token =

### Liveness: the process is up
GET {{api}}/healthz

### Readiness: Keycloak's signing keys and the FHIR server answer (503 when one does not)
GET {{api}}/readyz

### Who am I: identity, roles and the FHIR resource that is me
GET {{api}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token: 401 and a bare WWW-Authenticate challenge
GET {{api}}/api/me

### The panel: the patients the caller may see (a practitioner's panel, everyone for the admin)
GET {{api}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter by family name (a prefix, any case, accents ignored), sort and page
GET {{api}}/api/patients?family=garcia&sort=birthDate&limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One patient's demographics: your own, one on your panel, or anyone for the admin
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One screen about a patient: conditions, medication, allergies, latest vital signs, appointments, alerts
# A section that could not be loaded is null and named in "unavailable"; an empty one is [].
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A series: the readings of one measurement, newest first
# measurement is one of blood-pressure, heart-rate, spo2, glucose, weight, temperature. There is
# no offset and no total: "truncated" says the answer was cut at "limit" (default 100, at most 500).
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations?measurement=blood-pressure&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A period: "from" is inclusive, "to" is exclusive, a date means midnight UTC
# The demo readings cover the 30 days before you seeded: adjust the dates. In a query string a
# plain + means a space, so an offset is written %2B02:00 (or use Z).
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations?measurement=heart-rate&from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-15&sort=date
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Going further back: ask again with "to" set to the "at" of the oldest reading received
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations?measurement=heart-rate&limit=5&to=2026-10-12T08:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Record a reading: a patient for themselves, a clinician for their panel, the rules engine for anyone
# The unit is converted to the one the measurement is stored in (here mmol/L to mg/dL), and the
# time defaults to now. The patient, who took it and the id are decided by the server.
POST {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"measurement": "glucose", "value": 6.1, "unit": "mmol/L"}

### A blood pressure is two numbers; "at" is a time with its offset, at most 30 days ago
POST {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"measurement": "blood-pressure", "systolic": 128, "diastolic": 82, "at": "2026-10-14T08:00:00Z"}

### A reading that cannot be right: 422, with the fields that are wrong
# A Fahrenheit value labelled as Celsius is what the plausible limits are for.
POST {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"measurement": "temperature", "value": 98.6, "unit": "Cel"}

### A body of the wrong shape: 400, with the fields that are wrong
POST {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ana/observations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"measurement": "heart-rate"}

### The appointments the caller may see: a patient's own, those a practitioner takes part in, all for the admin
# status is proposed, booked or cancelled; sort is start or -start (a request with no time yet counts from the start of its window).
GET {{api}}/api/appointments?status=proposed&sort=start&limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A patient asks for an appointment with their general practitioner
# They say why and when they would like a time: a window of at most 30 days, as instants with an
# offset (a bare date is refused: whether "to 25 October" includes the 25th is not for the server to
# guess). The window must still be open, and start within 180 days. Dates here are examples: adjust.
POST {{api}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"description": "Blood pressure review", "requestedStart": "2026-10-20T00:00:00Z", "requestedEnd": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z"}

### A clinician confirms a request with a time (a practitioner takes part in it, or the admin)
# Replace the id with the one the request answered. A time lasts 5 minutes to 4 hours and is not in the past.
PATCH {{api}}/api/appointments/appt-sofia-1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "confirm", "start": "2026-10-21T09:00:00Z", "end": "2026-10-21T09:30:00Z"}

### ... moves a booked one
PATCH {{api}}/api/appointments/appt-sofia-1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "reschedule", "start": "2026-10-22T10:00:00Z", "end": "2026-10-22T10:45:00Z"}

### ... or cancels a proposed or a booked one, for a reason the patient can read
# A cancelled appointment is over: whatever is asked next is a 409 that names the status.
PATCH {{api}}/api/appointments/appt-sofia-1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "cancel", "reason": "The doctor is away that week"}

### A patient that does not exist: 404 for staff, 403 for a patient (no way to probe)
GET {{api}}/api/patients/pt-ghost
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### With a bad token: 401 and error="invalid_token"
GET {{api}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.token

### A request id of your own comes back on the response and in the logs
GET {{api}}/healthz
X-Request-Id: my-trace-1

### A route that does not exist: 404 as application/problem+json
GET {{api}}/nope

### A method the route does not support: 405 with Allow
POST {{api}}/healthz
